 kit policy - refuses a branch, subject, or title the policy forbids

   one of
   --input  prints the facts as JSON instead of judging them
   --facts  judges the facts document in <file>, and gathers nothing; for testing a rule against a
            fixture
   --rules  lists each rule the policy judges by: its name, its pattern, and where the pattern is
            set, as a table; it reads no forge and judges nothing. On a branch past the default it
            lists the base's rules, as kit policy judges by them, and fails as kit policy does when
            the base cannot be named or read


 kit policy
